# keur quality control — a function nested more than 3 control blocks deep.
#
# Why this exists: SonarCloud (S134) flagged keur's own code for exceeding 3
# nested control blocks (cmd/hook.cpp augment loop, common/platform_posix.cpp
# read_key). Deep nesting hides the happy path and multiplies the states a
# reader must hold. This rule makes S134 a keur-native check so the next deep
# nest is caught at commit time, not in CI — fix + control, the same way
# KEUR-ARCH-*/KEUR-PORT-* guard architecture and portability.
#
# HOW: the `max-nesting` engine (rules-authoring.md) tracks control-flow brace
# depth with a string/regex-aware lexer (shared with block-absence), counting
# only if/else/for/while/switch/do scopes. A function whose peak depth is > 3 is
# flagged once, at its opening line. Structs, lambdas and initializers do not
# count, so normal data code is quiet.
#
# WARN, not block: deep nesting is a maintainability smell, not a bug. It nudges
# toward guard clauses / extracting a helper. Tests are excluded (fixtures build
# deliberately nested shapes).
#
# @see docs/rules-authoring.md (`max-nesting`), SonarCloud cpp:S134.
id: KEUR-QUAL-004
ilities: [analysability]
maturity: 3
title: Function nested more than 3 control blocks deep
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: max-nesting
action: warn
min_count: 3
target:
  extensions: .c .cpp .cc .h .hpp
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ _test.cpp vendor/ build/ dist/
patterns:
  - regex: nesting too deep
    message: "Function nests more than 3 control blocks (if/for/while/switch) deep — hard to read and test. Flatten with guard clauses (early return/continue) or extract the inner work into a named helper. @see KEUR-QUAL-004, SonarCloud cpp:S134"
confidence: 0.6
fix: "Reduce control nesting to <=3: invert conditions into early return/continue guard clauses at the top, and extract the deepest block into a small named function. See docs/rules-authoring.md (max-nesting) and the augment_one_target / read_escape_tail extractions in cmd/hook.cpp and common/platform_posix.cpp."
